                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_40\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes StitchingExplorerPanel.java so that the unconditional statement\n\"savedFilteringAndGrouping = null;\" (which ran right after triggering the asynchronous\nglobal-optimization popup via globalOptPopup.doClick()) is moved into an \"else\" branch,\nso it only discards the saved SpimDataFilteringAndGrouping when global optimization was\nNOT triggered. Previously, the field was always nulled out immediately, even when global\noptimization was requested, so the asynchronous global-optimization task (which reads\nthe saved filtering/grouping later, on another thread) found it already discarded.\n\ncandidate_40 is the commit that originally introduced this entire mechanism: it adds the\n`savedFilteringAndGrouping` field to StitchingExplorerPanel, the `doGlobalOpt` flow that\ncalls `globalOptPopup.doClick()`, and immediately following it the unconditional\n\"// discard the temp. SpimDataFilteringAndGrouping / savedFilteringAndGrouping = null;\"\nline \u2014 exactly the buggy code path later corrected by the fix. It also adds the\ncorresponding getSavedFilteringAndGrouping()/setSavedFilteringAndGrouping() accessors and\nwires OptimizeGloballyPopupExpertBatch and the CalculatePC popups to use the saved\nfiltering/grouping, establishing the whole feature (and its race-condition bug) at once.\n\nNo candidate between 40 and 49 touches this code again \u2014 candidate_49's diff is in fact\nbyte-identical to the fix commit's diff, confirming it is the actual bug-fix commit\nincluded in the candidate range, not a separate bug-introducing change. This confirms\ncandidate_40 is the first (and only) commit that introduced the problematic unconditional\ndiscard of savedFilteringAndGrouping.\n"
